 reliability and latency disqualify this variant.' --variant-status compact_25 discarded 'Failed 5/13 development requests; valid cases still show semantic conflation.' --variant-status compact_31 discarded 'Superseded by stronger constraint-aware finalists; no winner at this stage.' --variant-status centrality discarded 'Useful candidate source, but standalone ranking was not the selected architecture.' --variant-status planned_union_fast31 discarded 'Superseded by compact packing and revised runtime; weak conjunctions and unverified generated reasons remain.' --variant-status baseline_union_fast31 discarded 'Efficient on already-covered requests but loses coverage on indirect or underspecified requests.' --variant-status planned_union_google_gemini_3_1_flash_lite_packing3 active 'Cheaper runner-up, competitive on many requests; weaker role/setting precision in selected cases and one fresh provider error. Historical ungated pools remain labeled in provenance.' --variant-status planned_union_google_gemini_3_flash_preview_packing3 discarded 'Retained as quality comparison; generating reasons adds latency, cost and unverified assurances.' --variant-status planned_union_google_gemini_3_flash_preview_packing3_ids discarded 'Earlier IDs configuration failed car-chase output length; failure retained.' --variant-status planned_union_google_gemini_3_flash_preview_packing3_ids_v2 discarded '900-token configuration later failed fresh restaurant request; superseded by explicit minimal reasoning and larger output budget.' --variant-status planned_union_google_gemini_3_flash_preview_packing3_ids_v3_minimal winner 'Selected practical quality-first default: stronger whole-request precision across rounds, 41/41 successful outputs under final runtime. Not strict dominance or perfect relevance.' --winner planned_union_google_gemini_3_flash_preview_packing3_ids_v3_minimal --summary 'Selected practical quality-first winner: semantic planning, pooled evidence and Flash minimal-reasoning IDs-only reranking. Evaluated on a 50,000-title sample across 41 unique requests; 20 were fresh confirmation/validation requests. Lite remains a cheaper, competitive runner-up. Final eight: 8/8 successful Flash runs, 5.24 s median reconstructed total, 19.03 s slowest; mean cost $0.005503 (median $0.005425). Earlier failed configurations and assistant disagreements are retained. This is a relative quality choice, not strict dominance, perfect relevance, or a production latency guarantee.'
